      "sample_index": 6,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of an angle whose measure is double the measure of its complement, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Let \\( x \\) be the measure of the angle.\n2. The complement of the angle is \\( 90^\\circ - x \\).\n3. According to the problem, the angle is double its complement, so we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   x = 2(90^\\circ - x)\n   \\]\n4. Now, solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = 180^\\circ - 2x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x + 2x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nSo, the measure of the angle is \\( 60^\\circ \\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure the accuracy of our solution.\n```python\n# Define the angle measure\nx = 60\n\n# Calculate the complement of the angle\ncomplement = 90 - x\n\n# Check if the angle is double its complement\nis_correct = (x == 2 * complement)\n\nprint((x, complement, is_correct))\n```\n```output\n(60, 30, True)\n```\nThe Python code confirms that the angle measure is \\( 60^\\circ \\), and its complement is \\( 30^\\circ \\). Since \\( 60^\\circ \\) is indeed double \\( 30^\\circ \\), the solution is correct.\n\nThus, the degree measure of the angle is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
